bgt:IssueCiGgenBinary a ghtf:RepoManagementInstance ;
    rdfs:label "issue: Install a real ggen binary in CI and drop continue-on-error from the GATE M2 determinism check" ;
    ghtf:instanceOf ghtf:GithubIssue ;
    ghtf:riskTier 2 ;
    ghtf:family "issues" ;
    ghtf:hclBody """resource "github_issue" "ci_ggen_binary" {
  repository = var.repository
  title      = "Install a real `ggen` binary in CI and drop continue-on-error from the GATE M2 determinism check"
  body       = <<EOT
The determinism-check step in `.github/workflows/beam4pm-ci.yml` runs `bash scripts/gate_m2_check.sh` under `continue-on-error: true` with an explicit KNOWN GAP comment:

> "this step needs a real `ggen` binary on the runner and none is installed here yet. It fails loudly ('ggen: command not found') instead of faking a pass; continue-on-error is set only so this one tracked gap does not turn every push/PR red. Remove continue-on-error once a real install step lands."

Source: `.github/workflows/beam4pm-ci.yml:71-80` (step starts line 71, `continue-on-error: true` line 72, KNOWN GAP comment lines 75-79, the `gate_m2_check.sh` invocation line 80).

Work: add a real `ggen` install step to the CI job (pinned version, matching what M0-M6 gate closure used: ggen 26.8.18 per `docs/jira/v26.8.29/16-gate-closure-m0-m6.md:43`), then remove `continue-on-error: true` so a real determinism regression fails the build instead of being silently tolerated.
EOT
  labels     = ["kind-ci-cd", "kind-infrastructure", "tech-github", "tech-ggen"]
}
""" .

bgt:IssueAlignBeamToolchainVersions a ghtf:RepoManagementInstance ;
    rdfs:label "issue: Align beam4pm-ci.yml's pinned BEAM toolchain versions with the versions the M0-M6 gate closure was actually verified against" ;
    ghtf:instanceOf ghtf:GithubIssue ;
    ghtf:riskTier 2 ;
    ghtf:family "issues" ;
    ghtf:hclBody """resource "github_issue" "align_beam_toolchain_versions" {
  repository = var.repository
  title      = "Align beam4pm-ci.yml's pinned BEAM toolchain versions with the versions the M0-M6 gate closure was actually verified against"
  body       = <<EOT
`.github/workflows/beam4pm-ci.yml:32-35` pins `otp-version: '27.2'` and `elixir-version: '1.18.5'` (gleam-version `'1.18.1'` matches).

But `docs/jira/v26.8.29/16-gate-closure-m0-m6.md:55-58` (GATE M3) records the real verification as:

> "Erlang: `erlc -Werror` clean, OTP 28.3.1. Elixir: `mix compile --warnings-as-errors --force` clean, Elixir 1.19.5. Gleam: `gleam build` warning-free, gleam 1.18.1."

CI is exercising a materially older OTP/Elixir pair (27.2/1.18.5) than the pair the crowned gate closure actually proved (28.3.1/1.19.5). Either bump the CI pins to match the verified pair, or add an explicit note in the workflow documenting the intentional divergence and why it's still considered covering.
EOT
  labels     = ["kind-ci-cd", "tech-github"]
}
""" .

